---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="OpenAjang">
  <section class="introduction">
    <h1>OpenAjang</h1>
    <p class="lead">A small JSON format for publishing public events at a URL.</p>
    <p>Write an event file, link to your registration form, and host it on your own website or a static host such as GitHub Pages. Compatible apps and directories can read it, display it, and check for changes.</p>
    <p class="status"><strong>Working draft, version 0.1.</strong> The format, examples, and local tools are available for experimentation. There is no requirement to join a central OpenAjang service.</p>
    <p class="project-links"><a class="button" href="/spec/">Read the specification</a> <a href="/validator/">Validator</a> <a href="https://github.com/nedpals/openajang">Source on GitHub</a></p>
  </section>

  <section id="try" class="demo">
    <h2>Try an event document</h2>
    <p>Fetch a direct JSON URL in your browser, or load the bundled illustrative fixture. Its details were not rechecked and may be outdated; it is not a live listing.</p>
    <form id="fetch-form">
      <label for="event-url">Event JSON URL</label>
      <div class="fetch-row"><input id="event-url" type="url" placeholder="https://example.org/event.openajang.json" required /><button type="submit">Fetch event</button></div>
      <div class="demo-actions"><button type="button" id="example">Load bundled example</button><button type="reset" class="reset">Clear</button></div>
    </form>
    <p class="hint">The remote host must allow browser access (CORS). This demo reads JSON URLs, not event pages; no server fetches them for you.</p>
    <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to fetch an event here. You can still <a href="/examples/">browse the examples</a> and read the specification.</p></noscript>
    <div id="event-result" aria-live="polite"><p>Enter a URL or load the example to see an event.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Why this exists</h2>
    <p>In my local tech community in Davao, I've seen organizations build their own event platforms while events continue to be announced across Facebook, community websites, and other event services. Each organizer has reasons for choosing where to publish: audience reach, control, cost, or simply what their volunteers can maintain.</p>
    <p>I ran into this while building <a href="https://naonao.ph">Naonao.ph</a>, an event platform for our small startup. We built useful features, but convincing organizers to maintain another event listing was still difficult. For participants, another account, another onboarding flow, and another place to remember created friction too.</p>
    <p>Could an event be published where its organizer already works, while people follow it through the tools they choose?</p>
    <p>OpenAjang explores that approach using ordinary web publishing: structured information at stable URLs, links between representations, and feeds for discovery. This depends on publishers exposing compatible data. It does not automatically extract events from Facebook or make an existing platform compatible.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>Each website publishes its own event documents. A participant can discover them through either route in the same compatible consumer:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Direct import:</strong> paste an event page or JSON URL into the app. The app retrieves the event from its publisher.</li>
      <li><strong>Feed discovery:</strong> subscribe to a directory's feed. The directory collects and refreshes events from multiple publishers; the app follows the feed's document links to retrieve structured event information.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Directories are optional. Registration takes participants to the organizer's chosen provider.</p>
    <p><a href="/feeds/">Read the feed guidance</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>For organizers</h2>
    <p>Publish an event document on hosting you choose and link to your existing registration process.</p>
    <p><a href="#publish">Publish your first event</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>For participants</h2>
    <p>Import an event into a compatible consumer, or discover events through a directory's feed. Ordinary feed readers can display event summaries and links.</p>
    <p><a href="/feeds/">Read about directory feeds</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>For developers</h2>
    <p><strong>Platform developers:</strong> export event documents and provide discovery links while continuing to offer your own management features.</p>
    <p><strong>Directory developers:</strong> fetch and validate events, retain source provenance, refresh them, and distribute links through feeds.</p>
    <p><a href="/spec/">Read the specification</a> or explore the <a href="https://github.com/nedpals/openajang/tree/master/packages/core">TypeScript SDK</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="publish"><h2>Publish your first event</h2><div class="publish">
    <div><ol><li><strong>Write</strong> an event JSON document.</li><li><strong>Host</strong> it at a public URL.</li><li><strong>Share</strong> the URL with compatible consumers or a directory.</li><li><strong>Maintain</strong> the source as details change.</li></ol><p>This example is illustrative; replace its details with your own.</p><a href="https://github.com/nedpals/openajang#publish-your-first-event">Full publishing guidance</a></div>
    <pre><code>{`{
  "$schema": "https://openajang.nedpals.xyz/schema/0.1/event.json",
  "type": "event",
  "url": "https://example.org/events/build-night",
  "title": "Community Build Night",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "starts_at": "2026-11-14T18:00:00+08:00",
  "organizer": { "name": "Example Community" },
  "location": {
    "type": "physical",
    "physical": { "name": "Community Hall, Davao" }
  },
  "updated_at": "2026-10-29T08:00:00Z"
}`}</code></pre>
  </div></section>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Why another format?</h2>
    <p>The <a href="https://xkcd.com/927/">xkcd standards problem</a> is a fair concern. <a href="https://schema.org/Event">Schema.org Event</a>, <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545">iCalendar</a>, and <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8984">JSCalendar</a> already represent much of this information. Their capabilities are not the missing ingredient.</p>
    <p>The hypothesis behind OpenAjang is narrower: a volunteer organizer or developer may find it easier to maintain one small, prescribed event document with direct registration fields and a predictable URL-import contract. It chooses one shape for common information and keeps specialized features outside the core.</p>
    <p>A simpler authoring experience is a design goal that needs testing with organizers, not a proven adoption advantage. The project earns its place only if it reduces publishing and integration work.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose"><h2>Try the draft</h2><p>Experiment with the <a href="/validator/">validator</a>, <a href="/spec/">specification</a>, and <a href="/examples/">examples</a>. The optional <a href="https://github.com/nedpals/openajang/tree/master/packages/core">TypeScript SDK</a> and <a href="https://github.com/nedpals/openajang/issues">feedback on GitHub</a> are open to everyone.</p></section>
</Base>
<script>
  import { Buffer } from 'buffer';
  globalThis.Buffer = Buffer;
  import { parseJsonStrict, validateSafe } from '@openajang/core';
  const form = document.querySelector('#fetch-form') as HTMLFormElement;
  const input = document.querySelector('#event-url') as HTMLInputElement;
  const result = document.querySelector('#event-result') as HTMLElement;
  const submit = form.querySelector('button[type=submit]') as HTMLButtonElement;
  let controller: AbortController | undefined;
  let generation = 0;
  const message = (text: string) => { result.replaceChildren(); const p = document.createElement('p'); p.textContent = text; result.append(p); };
  async function load(value: string) {
    controller?.abort(); const current = ++generation;
    let url: URL;
    try { url = new URL(value, location.href); if (!['http:', 'https:'].includes(url.protocol) || url.username || url.password) throw Error(); }
    catch { submit.disabled = false; message('Enter a valid HTTP or HTTPS JSON URL.'); return; }
    const requestController = new AbortController();
    controller = requestController;
    const timer = setTimeout(() => requestController.abort(), 10000);
    submit.disabled = true; message('Loading event…');
    try {
      const response = await fetch(url.href, { signal: requestController.signal, credentials: 'omit' });
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`The server returned HTTP ${response.status}.`);
      const reader = response.body?.getReader(); if (!reader) throw new Error('The response was empty.');
      const chunks: Uint8Array[] = []; let size = 0;
      while (true) { const {done, value} = await reader.read(); if (done) break; size += value.length; if (size > 1024 * 1024) { await reader.cancel(); throw new Error('The document exceeds the 1 MB limit.'); } chunks.push(value); }
      const bytes = new Uint8Array(size); let offset = 0; for (const chunk of chunks) { bytes.set(chunk, offset); offset += chunk.length; }
      const parsed = parseJsonStrict(new TextDecoder('utf-8', { fatal: true }).decode(bytes));
      const validation = validateSafe(parsed);
      if (!validation.valid) throw new Error(`Invalid OpenAjang event: ${validation.errors[0]?.message ?? 'validation failed'}`);
      if (current !== generation) return;
      const event = validation.event!;
      result.replaceChildren();
      if (url.pathname === '/examples/pycon-davao-2026.openajang.json' && url.origin === location.origin) {
        const notice = document.createElement('p');
        notice.textContent = 'Illustrative fixture, not a live listing. Details were not rechecked and may be outdated.';
        result.append(notice);
      }
      const heading = document.createElement('h3'); heading.textContent = event.title; result.append(heading);
      const add = (label: string, value: string | undefined) => { if (!value) return; const p = document.createElement('p'); p.textContent = `${label}: ${value}`; result.append(p); };
      add('Summary', event.summary); add('Status', event.status); add('Starts', event.starts_at); add('Ends', event.ends_at); add('Organizer', event.organizer?.name);
      const source = document.createElement('p'); source.textContent = `JSON source: ${response.url || url.href}`; result.append(source);
      try { const linkUrl = new URL(event.url); if (['http:', 'https:'].includes(linkUrl.protocol)) { const a = document.createElement('a'); a.href = linkUrl.href; a.textContent = 'Visit event page'; result.append(a); } } catch { /* no actionable URL */ }
    } catch (error) { if (current !== generation) return; message(error instanceof TypeError ? 'Could not fetch this URL. Check the address, network, and whether the host permits CORS.' : error instanceof Error && error.name === 'AbortError' ? 'The request timed out. Try again.' : `Could not read the event: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'unknown error'}`); }
    finally { clearTimeout(timer); if (current === generation) submit.disabled = false; }
  }
  form.addEventListener('submit', e => { e.preventDefault(); void load(input.value); });
  document.querySelector('#example')!.addEventListener('click', () => { input.value = new URL('/examples/pycon-davao-2026.openajang.json', location.href).href; void load(input.value); });
  form.addEventListener('reset', () => { ++generation; controller?.abort(); submit.disabled = false; message('Enter a URL or load the example to see an event.'); });
</script>
<style>
  section { margin: 2rem 0; }
  .introduction { margin: .5rem 0 1.75rem; max-width: 70ch; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .status { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }
  .project-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem 1.25rem; align-items: center; }
  .prose { max-width: 70ch; }
  .demo { background: var(--panel); padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; }
  .demo h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; }
  label { display: block; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: .35rem; }
  .fetch-row { display: flex; gap: .5rem; }
  .fetch-row input { flex: 1; min-width: 0; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .demo-actions { display: flex; gap: .5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: .65rem; }
  .demo-actions button { background: linear-gradient(var(--control-top), var(--control-bottom)); color: var(--fg); border-color: var(--line); font-size: .85rem; }
  .demo-actions button:hover { background: var(--code); border-color: var(--muted); }
  .hint { color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; margin: 1rem 0 .75rem; }
  #event-result { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: .75rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  #event-result h3 { margin: .5rem 0; }
  #event-result p { margin: .4rem 0; }
  .publish { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: start; }
  .publish pre { margin: 0; }
  li { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .publish ol { margin-top: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .fetch-row { flex-direction: column; }
    .publish { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .demo { padding: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
